// src/user/color/tonemap_kind.pdx -- G6-M5-001 (paideia-os #2238)
//
// KIND_TONEMAP_LUT = 0x1B6, derived over KIND_MEMORY (= slot 4 = KIND_PAGE).
//
// Design authority: design/roadmap/next-wave-softarch.md §G6 (color +
// HDR) row for KIND_TONEMAP_LUT plus the CICP triple this schema exposes
// per §G6.M1's KIND_COLOR_PROFILE tail (primaries/transfer/matrix, ITU-T
// H.273). This landing is the Wave 0 Batch 1 SCHEMA SEED: it registers
// the ordinal, publishes the 3D-LUT storage layout and CICP-tag namespace
// every downstream sampler / builder / composer will read from, and
// stubs the tetrahedral-interpolation sampler behind an INVOKE_UNSUPPORTED
// return.  The real cross-lattice sampler (BT.2408 SDR<->HDR curves)
// lands at G6-M5-002 and later G6 milestones -- see "Downstream" §.
//
// SLOT ALLOCATION.  0x1B6 is the next free derived-kind tag per
// design/architecture/next-wave-derived-kinds.md §"Summary counts and
// free bands" (see the 2026-08-31 entry).  The R101/R103/R104/R105 GUI
// block occupies 0x1AE..0x1B1, the R90-XREPO.LV11 wave took 0x1B2..0x1B4
// (KIND_SCHEMA_HANDLE / KIND_VOLUME_SNAPSHOT / KIND_KEK), and 0x1B6 is
// verified free by grep over src/kernel/core/cap/*.pdx as of this
// landing.  Main should reconcile the allocation table's "Next free
// derived-kind tag" line by advancing it to 0x1B6.
//
// DERIVATION.  Over KIND_MEMORY (= KIND_PAGE, 4).  Rationale: a
// tone-map LUT is a body of bytes with a schema tag on top -- exactly
// the shape KIND_COLOR_PROFILE and KIND_HDR_METADATA already use in the
// same G6 family.  The G6 planning skeleton in next-wave-softarch.md
// §857 originally listed KIND_TONEMAP_LUT as *derived over KIND_GPU_BO*;
// the issue's own directive (#2238) pins the base at KIND_MEMORY so the
// LUT schema is expressible without a GPU parent -- CPU-side tone-map
// paths, offline LUT builders, and reference-display validation all
// hold the LUT as a memory-backed cap and never need GPU authority.  A
// later G6 milestone MAY introduce a companion KIND_GPU_TONEMAP_LUT that
// derives from this schema plus a KIND_GPU_BO if the GPU compositor
// wants zero-copy sampling, but this landing does NOT prejudge that
// choice.  Main should confirm this base choice against the roadmap
// synthesis before wiring dispatch (an allocation-table clarification
// may be warranted).
//
// FINGERPRINT.  One legacy-suffixed mint fingerprint per the standard
// klog convention -- see feedback_paideia_as_reserved_labels-adjacent
// discipline used by kind_tls_trust / kind_tui_canvas.  Emitted once on
// successful mint by the future substrate; no fingerprint on the query
// or sample paths.
//
// LABEL PREFIX: `tmk_` (tonemap kind) throughout, sidestepping paideia-as
// reserved-word collisions (`loop`, `if`, `let`, `write`, ...).
//
// MECE SCOPE.  Single file under src/user/color/.  No mod.pdx exists in
// this directory yet; if main decides to add one, the registry marker
// `; wave0-b1-04: tonemap_kind` marks this module's slot.  No other
// file in src/user/color/ is touched here.
//
// =============================================================================
// SECTION 1 -- 3D-LUT STORAGE SCHEMA
// =============================================================================
//
// A tone-map LUT is a 3D cubic lattice indexed by (r, g, b) in some
// input color space, whose value is an output (r', g', b') triple in a
// different color space (or the same space with different transfer
// characteristics).  The lattice is stored as a flat, row-major, packed
// samples[N*N*N * 3] array where N is the per-axis grid size.
//
// Two grid sizes are admitted at this landing:
//
//   * TMK_GRID_17  -- 17 per axis => 4913 samples => 14739 values.
//     The industry-standard "medium" LUT; used by every major color
//     workflow (ACES, DaVinci Resolve, OCIO, ffmpeg zscale) as its
//     default.  Small enough to fit in L2 on every target CPU.
//
//   * TMK_GRID_33  -- 33 per axis => 35937 samples => 107811 values.
//     The "high-fidelity" LUT; matches the DoVi / HDR10+ reference
//     workflows and the CalMAN measurement grid.  Fits in L3.
//
// Two value encodings are admitted:
//
//   * TMK_ENC_FP16 (preferred) -- IEEE 754 half.  Native for HDR
//     linear-light values and BT.2408 SDR<->HDR mapping curves; the
//     encoding the sampler at G6-M5-002 will assume by default.
//
//   * TMK_ENC_U16  (alt)       -- 16-bit unsigned normalized [0, 1].
//     For LUTs generated from legacy 3D-LUT files (.cube / .3dl) whose
//     source data was already quantized; conversion to FP16 happens at
//     sample time, not at mint.
//
// The color-space tagging on input AND output axes uses the CICP triple
// (Coding-Independent Code Points, ITU-T H.273): primaries (u8),
// transfer characteristics (u8), matrix coefficients (u8).  This is the
// SAME namespace KIND_COLOR_PROFILE uses (see next-wave-softarch.md
// §593), so a tone-map LUT and a color profile are directly composable
// on CICP alone -- no rebinding required.
//
// Row layout (64 bytes, one cache line).  Following the kind_tui_canvas
// eight-word discipline:
//
//   [+0]  header:      in_use[63:56] | reserved[55:0]
//   [+8]  lut_id:      u64, kernel-assigned, never 0
//   [+16] memory_slot: u64, KIND_MEMORY(4) cap_table slot backing the
//                      packed samples[] array
//   [+24] axes_pack:   grid_size[63:56] | value_enc[55:48] |
//                      in_primaries[47:40]  | in_transfer[39:32] |
//                      in_matrix[31:24]     | out_primaries[23:16] |
//                      out_transfer[15:8]   | out_matrix[7:0]
//   [+32] direction_pack: direction[63:56] | sample_bytes[55:0]
//                         (direction: SDR->HDR, HDR->SDR, HDR->HDR;
//                          sample_bytes: N*N*N * 3 * enc_bytes,
//                          precomputed at mint for fast bound checks)
//   [+40] samples_touched: u64, running SAMPLE-op count
//   [+48] reserved0:   u64 (future: peak_luminance_nits u32 | matrix
//                      variant u8 | halo params u16)
//   [+56] reserved1:   u64 (future: BT.2408 curve id + saturation
//                      compression parameters)
//
// Value encoding of `axes_pack` is the canonical wire form.  It stays
// inside a single u64 so the mint gate can atomically publish it and
// so a future GPU-side handler can read it in one uncached load.

module TonemapKind = structure {

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.1 -- KIND ORDINAL + LAM-HINT BASE
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let KIND_TONEMAP_LUT      : u64 = 0x1B6
  pub let KIND_TONEMAP_LUT_BASE : u64 = 4       // = KIND_MEMORY (LAM-hint slot)

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.2 -- GRID AXIS SIZES (per-axis N)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Only 17 and 33 are admitted.  A future high-precision milestone MAY
  // add TMK_GRID_65 for 12-bit-target grading if needed; today's ceiling
  // is 33 to keep sample_bytes below 1 MiB (33^3 * 3 * 2 = 215622 B for
  // FP16, ~215 KiB) so the LUT always fits inside a single 2 MiB huge
  // page without straddling.

  pub let TMK_GRID_17 : u64 = 17
  pub let TMK_GRID_33 : u64 = 33
  pub let TMK_GRID_MAX : u64 = 33

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.3 -- VALUE ENCODINGS
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Numeric tag stored in axes_pack[55:48].  0 is reserved as the
  // invalid sentinel (mirrors kind_tls_trust's TLS_TRUST_ALGO_MAX
  // convention of never using 0 for a valid tag).

  pub let TMK_ENC_INVALID : u64 = 0
  pub let TMK_ENC_FP16    : u64 = 1
  pub let TMK_ENC_U16     : u64 = 2
  pub let TMK_ENC_MAX     : u64 = 2

  // Bytes per sample value under each encoding.  A "sample" is one
  // (r', g', b') triple = 3 values; a grid with N-per-axis holds
  // N*N*N samples * 3 values * enc_bytes total bytes.
  pub let TMK_ENC_BYTES_FP16 : u64 = 2
  pub let TMK_ENC_BYTES_U16  : u64 = 2

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.4 -- CICP TRIPLE (per-axis, input + output)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Values are the ITU-T H.273 code-points.  Only the values a G6
  // reference-display workflow actually emits are named here; the full
  // enumeration lives with KIND_COLOR_PROFILE at G6.M1.  Numeric tags
  // are the H.273 canonical values so a byte-for-byte match against a
  // CICP header from a decoder is a direct memcmp, not a translation.

  // Primaries (H.273 §8.1).
  pub let TMK_PRI_BT709        : u64 = 1
  pub let TMK_PRI_BT2020       : u64 = 9
  pub let TMK_PRI_DCI_P3       : u64 = 12
  pub let TMK_PRI_DISPLAY_P3   : u64 = 12   // shares 12; display vs DCI is a matrix distinction
  pub let TMK_PRI_MAX          : u64 = 22   // room to grow through H.273's 22 assigned codes

  // Transfer characteristics (H.273 §8.2).
  pub let TMK_TR_BT709         : u64 = 1
  pub let TMK_TR_LINEAR        : u64 = 8
  pub let TMK_TR_SRGB          : u64 = 13
  pub let TMK_TR_BT2020_10     : u64 = 14
  pub let TMK_TR_BT2020_12     : u64 = 15
  pub let TMK_TR_PQ            : u64 = 16    // SMPTE ST 2084 PQ
  pub let TMK_TR_HLG           : u64 = 18    // ARIB STD-B67 / BT.2100 HLG
  pub let TMK_TR_MAX           : u64 = 18

  // Matrix coefficients (H.273 §8.3).
  pub let TMK_MX_IDENTITY      : u64 = 0
  pub let TMK_MX_BT709         : u64 = 1
  pub let TMK_MX_BT601         : u64 = 6
  pub let TMK_MX_BT2020_NCL    : u64 = 9
  pub let TMK_MX_BT2020_CL     : u64 = 10
  pub let TMK_MX_ICTCP         : u64 = 14
  pub let TMK_MX_MAX           : u64 = 14

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.5 -- TONE-MAP DIRECTION
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Stored in direction_pack[63:56].  Semantics match the G6 milestone
  // planning (next-wave-softarch.md §595 delta: sdr_to_hdr / hdr_to_sdr /
  // hdr_to_hdr).  A fourth "identity" direction is reserved for
  // round-trip validation LUTs a future test-harness may want.

  pub let TMK_DIR_INVALID    : u64 = 0
  pub let TMK_DIR_SDR_TO_HDR : u64 = 1
  pub let TMK_DIR_HDR_TO_SDR : u64 = 2
  pub let TMK_DIR_HDR_TO_HDR : u64 = 3
  pub let TMK_DIR_IDENTITY   : u64 = 4    // reserved, test-only
  pub let TMK_DIR_MAX        : u64 = 4

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.6 -- ROW LAYOUT CONSTANTS
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let TMK_ROW_BYTES : u64 = 64
  pub let TMK_LUT_MAX   : u64 = 8            // pool ceiling, kind_tls_trust precedent

  // Offsets into the 64-byte row (see file header §"Row layout").
  pub let TMK_OFF_HEADER          : u64 = 0
  pub let TMK_OFF_LUT_ID          : u64 = 8
  pub let TMK_OFF_MEMORY_SLOT     : u64 = 16
  pub let TMK_OFF_AXES_PACK       : u64 = 24
  pub let TMK_OFF_DIRECTION_PACK  : u64 = 32
  pub let TMK_OFF_SAMPLES_TOUCHED : u64 = 40
  pub let TMK_OFF_RESERVED0       : u64 = 48
  pub let TMK_OFF_RESERVED1       : u64 = 56

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.7 -- RIGHTS
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Mirrors kind_tui_canvas / kind_tls_trust bit-assignment style.  A
  // tone-map LUT is read-mostly: SAMPLE is the hot path, INVOKE covers
  // the metadata queries, MINT reserved for a future authoring path,
  // REVOKE for teardown, OBSERVE for the debug printer.

  pub let R_TMK_SAMPLE  : u64 = 0x001    // tetrahedral sample (stubbed here)
  pub let R_TMK_INVOKE  : u64 = 0x008    // QUERY_GRID / QUERY_ENC / QUERY_CICP_*
  pub let R_TMK_MINT    : u64 = 0x200    // reserved; no v1 authoring path
  pub let R_TMK_REVOKE  : u64 = 0x010
  pub let R_TMK_OBSERVE : u64 = 0x400
  pub let R_TMK_ALL     : u64 = 0x619

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.8 -- OPS
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Dispatch itself lands in a future kernel-side cap_handler_tonemap_lut
  // milestone.  The tetrahedral sampler is stubbed at this landing --
  // see SECTION 3.

  pub let TMK_OP_SAMPLE           : u64 = 0    // (r,g,b) -> (r',g',b') via tetrahedral interp
  pub let TMK_OP_QUERY_GRID       : u64 = 1    // -> grid_size (17 or 33)
  pub let TMK_OP_QUERY_ENC        : u64 = 2    // -> value encoding tag
  pub let TMK_OP_QUERY_DIRECTION  : u64 = 3    // -> tone-map direction
  pub let TMK_OP_QUERY_IN_CICP    : u64 = 4    // -> (primaries|transfer|matrix) for INPUT
  pub let TMK_OP_QUERY_OUT_CICP   : u64 = 5    // -> (primaries|transfer|matrix) for OUTPUT
  pub let TMK_OP_QUERY_ID         : u64 = 6    // -> lut_id
  pub let TMK_OP_QUERY_MEMORY_ID  : u64 = 7    // -> memory_slot
  pub let TMK_OP_DEBUG_PRINT      : u64 = 8    // R_TMK_OBSERVE; row-fields dump
  pub let TMK_OP_MAX              : u64 = 8

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.9 -- FAILURE TAXONOMY
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // A fresh 16-wide band: 0xFFFFEB30..0xFFFFEB3F, disjoint from every
  // documented KIND_TTY (0xFFFFEC30..0xFFFFEC3F), KIND_TUI_CANVAS
  // (0xFFFFEB10..0xFFFFEB1F), KIND_TLS_TRUST (0xFFFFEB20..0xFFFFEB27),
  // and KIND_NIC (0xFFFFEB28..0xFFFFEB2F) band.  0xFFFFEB30..0xFFFFEB3F
  // is verified free by grep over src/kernel/core/cap/*.pdx +
  // tests/**/*.pdx as of this landing.

  pub let TMK_OK                    : u64 = 0
  pub let TMK_MINT_BAD_MEMORY       : u64 = 0xFFFFEB3F
  pub let TMK_MINT_BAD_GRID         : u64 = 0xFFFFEB3E
  pub let TMK_MINT_BAD_ENC          : u64 = 0xFFFFEB3D
  pub let TMK_MINT_BAD_DIRECTION    : u64 = 0xFFFFEB3C
  pub let TMK_MINT_BAD_IN_CICP      : u64 = 0xFFFFEB3B
  pub let TMK_MINT_BAD_OUT_CICP     : u64 = 0xFFFFEB3A
  pub let TMK_MINT_BAD_SIZE         : u64 = 0xFFFFEB39
  pub let TMK_TAIL_ENOSPC           : u64 = 0xFFFFEB38
  pub let TMK_BAD_SLOT              : u64 = 0xFFFFEB37
  pub let TMK_BAD_RIGHTS            : u64 = 0xFFFFEB36
  pub let TMK_SAMPLE_UNSUPPORTED    : u64 = 0xFFFFEB35   // stub return, this landing
  pub let TMK_REVOKE_ALREADY        : u64 = 0xFFFFEB34
  pub let TMK_DECODE_BAD            : u64 = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.10 -- STATS COUNTER SLOTS
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // The kernel-side substrate will publish a _tmk_stats [u64; 8] table;
  // the slot indices are named here so cross-module bumpers agree.

  pub let TMK_ST_MINTS    : u64 = 0
  pub let TMK_ST_REVOKES  : u64 = 1
  pub let TMK_ST_SAMPLES  : u64 = 2
  pub let TMK_ST_QUERIES  : u64 = 3
  pub let TMK_ST_REFUSED  : u64 = 4
  pub let TMK_ST_MAX      : u64 = 8

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1.11 -- FINGERPRINT (one line, legacy-suffixed)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Emitted once on successful mint by the future substrate.  The
  // legacy-suffix convention is what tools/verify-fingerprint-coverage.sh
  // enumerates, so this literal is the machine-checkable name of the
  // milestone.  No fingerprint on the query / sample / revoke paths.
  pub let tmk_mint_ok_msg : [u8; 50] = "tonemap lut mint ok [legacy: TONEMAP LUT MINT OK]\0"
  pub let tmk_k_lut_id    : [u8; 7]  = "lut_id\0"

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 2 -- PACKERS + VALIDATORS (schema-only, pure leaves)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Every function in this section is a pure, unsafe-bodied leaf with
  // small immediates (no MOVABS r64, imm64 anywhere), returns its
  // result in rax, and clobbers only rax + one scratch register.  This
  // is the encoder-conservative pattern kind_tls_trust / kind_tui_canvas
  // established -- no wide immediates, no push/pop, no nested calls.

  // tmk_grid_valid(g) -> 1 iff g in {17, 33}.
  pub let tmk_grid_valid : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (g: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G6-M5-001 (#2238): grid axis size validator.  Two admitted values: TMK_GRID_17=17 and TMK_GRID_33=33.  Straight compare + branch; small immediates so no MOVABS.  Labels prefixed tmk_gv_.",
      block: {
        cmp rdi, 17;
        je  tmk_gv_yes;
        cmp rdi, 33;
        je  tmk_gv_yes;
        xor rax, rax;
        ret;
      tmk_gv_yes:
        mov rax, 1;
        ret
      }
    }

  // tmk_enc_valid(e) -> 1 iff e in [1, TMK_ENC_MAX=2].
  pub let tmk_enc_valid : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (e: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G6-M5-001 (#2238): value-encoding validator.  Admits 1 (FP16) or 2 (U16); 0 is TMK_ENC_INVALID.  Labels prefixed tmk_ev_.",
      block: {
        cmp rdi, 1;
        jb  tmk_ev_no;
        cmp rdi, 2;
        ja  tmk_ev_no;
        mov rax, 1;
        ret;
      tmk_ev_no:
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // tmk_direction_valid(d) -> 1 iff d in [1, TMK_DIR_MAX=4].
  pub let tmk_direction_valid : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (d: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G6-M5-001 (#2238): tone-map direction validator.  Admits 1..4 (SDR_TO_HDR, HDR_TO_SDR, HDR_TO_HDR, IDENTITY reserved).  Labels prefixed tmk_dv_.",
      block: {
        cmp rdi, 1;
        jb  tmk_dv_no;
        cmp rdi, 4;
        ja  tmk_dv_no;
        mov rax, 1;
        ret;
      tmk_dv_no:
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // tmk_primaries_valid(p) -> 1 iff p in [1, TMK_PRI_MAX=22].
  pub let tmk_primaries_valid : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (p: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G6-M5-001 (#2238): CICP primaries validator.  Admits 1..22 (H.273 assigned range).  0 is the reserved-not-a-value sentinel; the sampler needs a concrete primaries choice to know the input gamut.  Labels prefixed tmk_pv_.",
      block: {
        cmp rdi, 1;
        jb  tmk_pv_no;
        cmp rdi, 22;
        ja  tmk_pv_no;
        mov rax, 1;
        ret;
      tmk_pv_no:
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // tmk_transfer_valid(t) -> 1 iff t in [1, TMK_TR_MAX=18].
  pub let tmk_transfer_valid : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (t: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G6-M5-001 (#2238): CICP transfer characteristics validator.  Admits 1..18 (spans BT.709 through HLG).  Labels prefixed tmk_tv_.",
      block: {
        cmp rdi, 1;
        jb  tmk_tv_no;
        cmp rdi, 18;
        ja  tmk_tv_no;
        mov rax, 1;
        ret;
      tmk_tv_no:
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // tmk_matrix_valid(m) -> 1 iff m in [0, TMK_MX_MAX=14].
  // Note: matrix 0 (identity) is VALID here -- a linear-light LUT
  // typically carries an identity matrix on both axes.
  pub let tmk_matrix_valid : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (m: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G6-M5-001 (#2238): CICP matrix coefficients validator.  Admits 0..14 (0 = identity, valid on a linear-light LUT).  Labels prefixed tmk_mv_.",
      block: {
        cmp rdi, 14;
        ja  tmk_mv_no;
        mov rax, 1;
        ret;
      tmk_mv_no:
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // tmk_axes_pack(grid_size, enc, in_pri, in_tr, in_mx, out_pri) ->
  // 48 low bits packed per the row layout at [+24].  out_tr and out_mx
  // MUST be packed by the caller via a second helper (SysV budget is 6
  // args; splitting keeps every packer within the register window).
  //
  // Layout inside the returned word (only [47:0] populated; caller ORs
  // with a second word from tmk_axes_pack_out for the full u64):
  //   grid_size[47:40] | enc[39:32] | in_pri[31:24] | in_tr[23:16] |
  //   in_mx[15:8]      | out_pri[7:0]
  pub let tmk_axes_pack_in : (u64, u64, u64, u64, u64, u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (grid_size: u64) (enc: u64) (in_pri: u64) (in_tr: u64) (in_mx: u64) (out_pri: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G6-M5-001 (#2238): pack six of the eight axes-pack fields into bits [47:0].  Every field masked to 8 bits before the shift so an out-of-range argument cannot smear into a neighbor.  Six SysV args (rdi/rsi/rdx/rcx/r8/r9); no push, no call.  Labels prefixed tmk_apn_ (none needed, straight-line).",
      block: {
        mov rax, r9;               // out_pri
        and rax, 0xFF;

        mov r10, r8;               // in_mx
        and r10, 0xFF;
        shl r10, 8;
        or  rax, r10;

        mov r10, rcx;              // in_tr
        and r10, 0xFF;
        shl r10, 16;
        or  rax, r10;

        mov r10, rdx;              // in_pri
        and r10, 0xFF;
        shl r10, 24;
        or  rax, r10;

        mov r10, rsi;              // enc
        and r10, 0xFF;
        shl r10, 32;
        or  rax, r10;

        mov r10, rdi;              // grid_size
        and r10, 0xFF;
        shl r10, 40;
        or  rax, r10;
        ret
      }
    }

  // tmk_axes_pack_out(out_tr, out_mx) -> word with only [15:8]|[7:0]
  // populated (out_tr in [15:8], out_mx in [7:0]).  Caller shifts left
  // by 48 and ORs with tmk_axes_pack_in's result to form the full row
  // word at [+24].
  pub let tmk_axes_pack_out : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (out_tr: u64) (out_mx: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G6-M5-001 (#2238): pack the trailing two axes-pack fields (out_tr, out_mx) into bits [15:0] of a u64.  Caller shifts left 48 and ORs with tmk_axes_pack_in's result.  Labels prefixed tmk_apo_ (none needed).",
      block: {
        mov rax, rsi;              // out_mx
        and rax, 0xFF;

        mov r10, rdi;              // out_tr
        and r10, 0xFF;
        shl r10, 8;
        or  rax, r10;
        ret
      }
    }

  // tmk_direction_pack(direction, sample_bytes) -> direction[63:56] |
  // sample_bytes[55:0].  sample_bytes is the caller-computed
  // N*N*N * 3 * enc_bytes; caps at 56 bits (72 PB) so a validator can
  // reject an overflowed multiply.
  pub let tmk_direction_pack : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (direction: u64) (sample_bytes: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G6-M5-001 (#2238): pack direction[63:56] | sample_bytes[55:0] per row layout at [+32].  sample_bytes MASKED to 56 bits so a caller with a pathological value cannot smear into the direction field; the mint gate is expected to reject such inputs upstream via TMK_MINT_BAD_SIZE.  Labels prefixed tmk_dp_ (none needed).",
      block: {
        // r10 = sample_bytes & 0x00FFFFFFFFFFFFFF
        mov r10, rsi;
        // Encoder-conservative build of the 56-bit mask: shl+shr trick
        // avoids MOVABS r64, imm64 (a bare 0x00FFFFFFFFFFFFFF).
        shl r10, 8;
        shr r10, 8;

        mov rax, rdi;              // direction
        and rax, 0xFF;
        shl rax, 56;
        or  rax, r10;
        ret
      }
    }

  // tmk_hdr_pack() -> canonical row header (in_use bit set by the
  // mint gate's tail_alloc, not here).  Mirror of kind_tui_canvas's
  // tui_hdr_pack: returns 0 today.
  pub let tmk_hdr_pack : () -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G6-M5-001 (#2238): canonical row header.  Only in_use is ever written (by tail_alloc), low 56 bits stay 0.  Mirrors kind_tui_canvas.pdx tui_hdr_pack.  Labels prefixed tmk_hp_ (none needed).",
      block: {
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 3 -- TETRAHEDRAL-INTERPOLATION SAMPLING STUB
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // The real tetrahedral sampler decomposes each unit cube into 6
  // tetrahedra by the standard 3D-LUT convention (see the BT.2408
  // reference implementation and the OCIO 3D-LUT sampler): identify
  // which tet (r, g, b) falls in by their coordinate ordering; linearly
  // interpolate over the tet's four vertices.  That body needs FP16
  // load / decompress / weight / accumulate paths that G6-M5-002
  // introduces alongside the BT.2408 SDR<->HDR curve tables -- both
  // land as one coordinated milestone.  Until then, every dispatch of
  // TMK_OP_SAMPLE returns TMK_SAMPLE_UNSUPPORTED so downstream harnesses
  // observe a well-formed refusal rather than a fabricated value.
  //
  // Contract: tmk_sample_stub(row_id, r_q16, g_q16, b_q16, out_ptr)
  //   * row_id: cap_table slot for the LUT (unchecked at this stub).
  //   * r_q16, g_q16, b_q16: input coordinates in Q0.16 fixed-point
  //     ([0, 1] mapped to [0, 65535]); the sampler at G6-M5-002 will
  //     accept fp32 too, but Q16 keeps the stub's signature encoder-safe.
  //   * out_ptr: buffer for the (r', g', b') triple; ignored at stub.
  //   * Return: always TMK_SAMPLE_UNSUPPORTED (0xFFFFEB35).
  //
  // The out_ptr is deliberately NOT written by this stub -- writing a
  // fabricated triple would let a caller that ignores the return code
  // silently proceed with garbage.  Leaving out_ptr untouched keeps
  // any subsequent consumer of that buffer honest.

  pub let tmk_sample_stub : (u64, u64, u64, u64, u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (row_id: u64) (r_q16: u64) (g_q16: u64) (b_q16: u64) (out_ptr: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G6-M5-001 (#2238): tetrahedral sampler STUB.  Always returns TMK_SAMPLE_UNSUPPORTED (0xFFFFEB35).  Does NOT write out_ptr -- fabricated output would defeat the point of a well-formed refusal.  Real sampler lands at G6-M5-002 alongside BT.2408 SDR<->HDR curves.  Small immediate (32-bit sign-safe: 0xFFFFEB35 fits into 32 bits, so mov r64, imm32 sign-extends to a valid u64 sentinel).  Labels prefixed tmk_ss_ (none needed, straight-line).",
      block: {
        mov rax, 0xFFFFEB35;
        ret
      }
    }
}
